1
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:29,000
Get home safe.

2
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:30,640
She's pretty, huh?

3
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:32,880
You like her?
If you like her, that's better.

4
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:35,080
I don't want you messing with his woman.

5
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:38,320
Didn't you say if you had to choose
between me and boxing,

6
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:39,600
you'd choose me?

7
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:40,720
I want to choose you too.

8
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:43,080
But with everything happening now,
I can't do that.

9
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:44,840
Then he'll never quit.

10
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:48,720
If his life got better,
even if it meant doing wrong,

11
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:50,680
I think he'd accept it.

12
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:53,840
We agreed not to get involved with drugs.

13
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:57,560
That's why we're on our own.

14
00:01:57,640 --> 00:01:59,160
I promise

15
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:02,320
I'll take responsibility
for what happened to your mom.

16
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:05,200
Why do you keep coming here so often?

17
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:07,840
I need to talk to you.

18
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:09,280
From what I've heard,

19
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:12,120
there's no chance
we'll make it back alive.

20
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:21,480
- Hey.
- What?

21
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:23,520
You were done that fast?

22
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,200
Anyone coming for liquor today?

23
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:30,400
Yeah. Take two crates out front for me.

24
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:36,080
Hey, Pong. Today…

25
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:38,040
Whoa!

26
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,400
What the hell are you doing?

27
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:41,480
Dum!

28
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:43,920
What's going on? Hey, Pong.

29
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:46,560
Calm down. What did Dom do to you?

30
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:48,960
Ask him yourself.

31
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:50,840
What happened, Dom?

32
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:59,080
He won't answer,
but I know what he got Oab involved in.

33
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:04,000
You two should talk it out. Calm down.

34
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:07,520
We're family here.
If he could tell us, he would've already.

35
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,640
You're coming with me.

36
00:03:30,120 --> 00:03:31,080
Dum.

37
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,720
Is it okay to leave them alone?

38
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:38,440
You can't ask me about that.

39
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:40,280
I knew it. I can't trust you.

40
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:42,400
What are you doing?

41
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:46,000
I'm just doing what he told me to do.

42
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,440
Why would he order you to do it?

43
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:50,360
Well, maybe no one else could do it.

44
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:53,280
You bastard. Are you saying I'm useless?

45
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:56,040
If someone else could do it,

46
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:58,400
would he have chosen me?

47
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,480
That's what bothers me.

48
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,400
Why could you do it?
How did you get close to Liang?

49
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:10,080
- I guess I'm good with people.
- Good with people, my ass.

50
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:13,280
You were one of his people from the start.

51
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:15,480
If I was Liang's man from the beginning,

52
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:17,600
I wouldn't have been beaten
half to death like this.

53
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:32,280
I really can't talk about this.
Ask Oab yourself.

54
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:40,880
Can you give me a straight answer?

55
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:54,520
Yeah. Liang agreed to work for us.

56
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:57,360
And you accepted his terms?

57
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:05,880
No wonder it was so easy.

58
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:11,320
You were willing to spit
on your own dignity, so what can I say?

59
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:14,560
I know you don't agree with me, Pong.
But can you hear me out?

60
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:22,040
Why do you want to arrest Oab?

61
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,760
CASE TIMELINE: JULY 1991

62
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:25,400
What makes you think that?

63
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:32,400
There are plenty of people
with more influence than him.

64
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:36,400
We have evidence that he is selling drugs.

65
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:40,120
How could there be? If there was,
you would've arrested him already.

66
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:43,800
Dom has been inside for months
and still couldn't find anything.

67
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:46,640
I think

68
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:48,960
Dom just hasn't found it yet.

69
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,560
Otherwise, how could a drug dealer
get taken out in Oab's territory

70
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:56,920
if he wasn't involved?
Those powerful figures

71
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:59,480
don't step on each other's turf.
You know that.

72
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:02,720
Then what about Boss Peng?

73
00:06:03,320 --> 00:06:04,600
Why haven't you arrested him?

74
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:10,040
There's no evidence or witnesses
to arrest him.

75
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:13,680
But the CIB just arrested
drug dealers in his area.

76
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,280
It's the same with Oab.

77
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:18,640
Without evidence, without witnesses,

78
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:21,720
without catching him with drugs,
how can we arrest him?

79
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:29,040
Do you think I'm targeting him?

80
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:35,080
No. I just want to know
why you're trying to arrest Oab

81
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:37,640
when there's no clear evidence
that he's selling drugs.

82
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:39,400
Unlike Boss Peng's territory,

83
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:42,880
where drugs are everywhere,
yet you still haven't arrested him.

84
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:48,880
If there's evidence, we arrest them all.
We don't pick and choose.

85
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:05,960
This is only a day
after Arm's anniversary.

86
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:07,840
I know what I'm doing.

87
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:10,920
I already told Liang
about the plan I told you.

88
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:13,160
Everything will go as we discussed.

89
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,200
Dom's only job is to fight.

90
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:18,280
That's it.

91
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:21,880
I think your plan is way too risky.

92
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:25,400
- I know.
- I already told him that.

93
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:33,320
We're all going to end up dead.

94
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:35,880
He's the one who's going to die, not us.

95
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:38,760
Just be ready.

96
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,000
Where are you going?

97
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:04,560
I have something to do.

98
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:06,560
Going to pick up Fon?

99
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:08,680
She's not off work yet.

100
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:10,840
- I'll come with you.
- Alone.

101
00:08:34,799 --> 00:08:37,480
Since you came back,
Pong hasn't talked to anyone.

102
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,240
I don't know, Dum.

103
00:08:44,039 --> 00:08:46,560
Hey, what did you talk about with Oab?

104
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:49,560
- Just normal stuff.
- Really?

105
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:51,680
That's such a shameless lie.

106
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:53,520
If you don't want to tell us, just say so.

107
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:55,680
Come on. If you want to know, go ask Pong.

108
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:57,240
What? Are you messing with me, Dom?

109
00:08:57,320 --> 00:09:00,280
If I could tell you, I would.
So please stop asking.

110
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:01,480
Damn.

111
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:03,240
You've got a lot of secrets.

112
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:07,840
Who's that?

113
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:15,960
Dom.

114
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:17,800
Your customer is here.

115
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:19,640
Shit.

116
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:32,200
Are you here alone?

117
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:34,080
Yeah.

118
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:36,800
I came here looking for some company.

119
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:41,960
Please, have a seat.

120
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:53,520
- Haw.
- Yes, Dum.

121
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:55,120
- Haw.
- Yes?

122
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:58,400
At first I was wondering
why you said it was Dom's customer.

123
00:09:58,480 --> 00:09:59,760
And now?

124
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:04,080
I was away at the den for a little while,
and you guys have improved a lot.

125
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:06,240
Here's the menu.

126
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:12,360
You only have one brand of liquor here?

127
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:14,200
Yes.

128
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:17,960
No imported liquor?

129
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:21,680
If you prefer imported liquor,
try another place.

130
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:26,440
I prefer Thai liquor.

131
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:36,560
By the glass or by the bottle?

132
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:38,280
A bottle.

133
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:41,680
Have someone ready
to mix my drinks at the table.

134
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:55,320
Her again?

135
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:57,840
Yeah.

136
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:00,680
So she's the one.

137
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:02,160
Of course she is.

138
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:11,560
Boss Fon sounds pretty good, you know.

139
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:12,960
Really?

140
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:20,680
I'm just rooting for you.

141
00:11:20,760 --> 00:11:22,400
Whether it's good or bad,
I'll say it's good.

142
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:29,400
Go back to her. I'll go check the stock.

143
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:40,640
What are you thinking about?

144
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:47,480
A lot of things.

145
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:50,080
I understand.

146
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,280
When Arm was taken out,

147
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:58,040
all I could think about was revenge.

148
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:01,000
I wanted to kill Peng myself.

149
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:03,240
It's been a year.

150
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:07,560
I still haven't been able to do anything.

151
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:10,320
Why?

152
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,920
You're a cop, Fon. You should know.

153
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,280
If you have connections, you're safe.

154
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:25,520
If those connections are with the police,
it's even harder to touch them.

155
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:30,240
Do you know who's helping him?

156
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:32,640
I don't know.

157
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:35,600
But I'm sure there's someone, Fon.

158
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:43,680
From Boss Joe's bar.

159
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:49,080
Have you decided
whether you'll let Man fight yet?

160
00:12:49,160 --> 00:12:51,040
He still hasn't said who he's putting up.

161
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:53,200
I heard he's got a new fighter.

162
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:54,360
Who?

163
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:56,880
A temple fair boxer.

164
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:06,240
He's putting a temple fair boxer
against a former runner-up?

165
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:07,480
Huh?

166
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:09,640
If that's true,

167
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:12,920
he's either stupid or crazy.

168
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:20,800
But I think he's just trying
to humiliate me.

169
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:23,120
What are you going to do, Boss?

170
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:26,560
I think it's a good thing.

171
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:29,680
If Man loses to this new kid,

172
00:13:29,760 --> 00:13:31,160
his career is over.

173
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:37,440
You'll send Man in to lose?

174
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:39,800
Of course.

175
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:43,320
Pong.

176
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,000
Pong.

177
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:49,120
Dum.

178
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:50,920
What is it?

179
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:53,840
Why did Dom
serve the same table all night?

180
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:56,000
She paid well.

181
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:18,000
Don't your legs get tired?

182
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:24,760
You're no fun to drink with.

183
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:28,880
If you're not enjoying it,
I suggest you try another bar.

184
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:36,600
Fine, I don't need a seat.

185
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:39,440
Hey, get me another glass.

186
00:14:40,040 --> 00:14:41,000
Yes.

187
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:43,600
Take it to her.

188
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:47,080
Here you go.

189
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:07,560
If you won't sit,
then stand and drink with me.

190
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:11,400
We don't allow employees
to drink while they're working.

191
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:29,800
Why?

192
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:34,920
Do they also ban customers
from kissing staff on duty?

193
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:40,080
Dom, go take Pong home.

194
00:15:40,160 --> 00:15:41,360
He's drunk.

195
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:48,600
But I paid him to keep mixing drinks
until his shift ends.

196
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:50,200
His shift is over.

197
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:29,040
Can you stay here forever?

198
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:32,600
I can't.

199
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:30,920
Can I take care of you
for the rest of my life?

200
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:48,680
I've spent days thinking

201
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:51,400
about how to say this properly. But…

202
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:55,520
Now that the moment is here,
I can't say anything right.

203
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,080
- Oab, I…
- Fon.

204
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:10,560
I love you so much.

205
00:19:04,400 --> 00:19:05,520
Can we get back together?

206
00:20:02,840 --> 00:20:04,040
Oab.

207
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:05,680
My family just had a funeral.

208
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:08,840
I don't want people
to think I'm celebrating

209
00:20:08,920 --> 00:20:10,320
right after my mother's death.

210
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:16,160
We…

211
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:18,840
don't have to rush anything.

212
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:21,600
We can take it slowly.

213
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:24,520
I just want to

214
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:27,640
be engaged to you for now.

215
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:32,360
When you're ready,

216
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:35,640
we can talk about marriage.

217
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:40,720
Okay.

218
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:43,960
Until I'm ready.

219
00:24:12,440 --> 00:24:14,000
- Dum. You know what?
- Yeah?

220
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:15,760
Remember when you asked him
to take me home?

221
00:24:16,360 --> 00:24:18,880
- Guess how he did it.
- How?

222
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:23,920
He just dumped me there.
I woke up outside in the sun.

223
00:24:29,480 --> 00:24:30,960
He's not focused at all.

224
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:33,080
All he does is attack.
He doesn't even dodge.

225
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:35,560
How the hell is he supposed
to beat Man like that?

226
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:37,080
They're in different leagues. Look at him.

227
00:24:38,440 --> 00:24:40,320
You don't listen to me at all.

228
00:24:43,520 --> 00:24:44,560
Hey, where's your guard?

229
00:24:50,320 --> 00:24:52,600
- Hey! Stop!
- Hey!

230
00:24:55,040 --> 00:24:56,920
Back to your corners.

231
00:25:00,240 --> 00:25:01,320
Get over here, Dom.

232
00:25:03,320 --> 00:25:06,280
Hey! Dom.

233
00:25:06,360 --> 00:25:08,320
What's wrong with you today?

234
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:10,800
He countered you once
and you almost went down.

235
00:25:10,880 --> 00:25:14,440
Are you not going to guard at all today?
Focus, man.

236
00:25:14,520 --> 00:25:18,040
At this rate, just let him hit you.
What kind of sloppy fighting is this?

237
00:25:19,320 --> 00:25:20,360
Here.

238
00:25:21,600 --> 00:25:23,040
What's wrong with you today?

239
00:25:24,480 --> 00:25:25,560
Nothing.

240
00:25:31,640 --> 00:25:32,920
That's enough for today.

241
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:36,880
Hey.

242
00:25:37,600 --> 00:25:38,640
Dom.

243
00:25:48,280 --> 00:25:50,040
You fought like shit today.

244
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:54,080
What's wrong with you?

245
00:25:55,200 --> 00:25:56,480
You had no form at all.

246
00:25:56,560 --> 00:25:58,600
If you're tired, just tell me.

247
00:26:00,720 --> 00:26:03,000
I won't mind if you take a day off.

248
00:26:10,480 --> 00:26:11,440
No, I'm fine.

249
00:26:15,880 --> 00:26:17,320
If you fight like this,

250
00:26:19,520 --> 00:26:23,600
whether it's on the street, at a fair,
or at Lumpinee, you'll never win.

251
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:27,440
Ask yourself honestly.

252
00:26:27,520 --> 00:26:29,040
Do you really want to win?

253
00:26:34,360 --> 00:26:35,440
Yes.

254
00:26:36,560 --> 00:26:37,480
Good.

255
00:26:38,480 --> 00:26:41,320
- Tell him to dress properly and drive me.
- Yes.

256
00:26:43,320 --> 00:26:44,160
Hey, Dom.

257
00:26:45,880 --> 00:26:47,720
- Dom.
- What?

258
00:26:47,800 --> 00:26:50,440
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine.

259
00:26:51,440 --> 00:26:54,360
But today you really

260
00:26:54,440 --> 00:26:56,320
did fight like shit, just like he said.

261
00:26:57,520 --> 00:26:58,440
I know.

262
00:26:59,920 --> 00:27:01,120
Are you mad at him?

263
00:27:07,240 --> 00:27:08,600
I'm his subordinate.

264
00:27:10,360 --> 00:27:12,160
How could I be mad at him?

265
00:27:15,560 --> 00:27:16,640
It's about Fon, isn't it?

266
00:27:22,200 --> 00:27:24,080
I don't even want to look at his face.

267
00:27:25,240 --> 00:27:27,240
Yeah, just hang in there.

268
00:27:28,120 --> 00:27:31,960
He told me to tell you to dress up
and drive him today.

269
00:27:32,560 --> 00:27:34,440
He even told me
to make sure you dress properly.

270
00:27:48,160 --> 00:27:49,880
- Sorry.
- Sorry.

271
00:27:49,960 --> 00:27:51,880
You can get on first. I'll pick it up.

272
00:27:53,840 --> 00:27:54,960
Too late.

273
00:27:56,720 --> 00:27:58,440
AMON SOMPHAKUL

274
00:27:59,200 --> 00:28:00,600
Are you handling this case?

275
00:28:01,200 --> 00:28:02,040
Why do you ask?

276
00:28:02,640 --> 00:28:03,680
I used to work on this case.

277
00:28:06,880 --> 00:28:08,520
Then why was it never closed?

278
00:28:10,160 --> 00:28:12,200
It was entirely connected
to powerful figures.

279
00:28:14,600 --> 00:28:15,880
That's why it couldn't be closed?

280
00:28:18,160 --> 00:28:19,040
Boss Oab reported

281
00:28:19,120 --> 00:28:21,840
that his younger brother
was killed by Boss Peng.

282
00:28:22,720 --> 00:28:26,080
The officer who took the report
gathered the evidence and sent it to me.

283
00:28:26,160 --> 00:28:29,440
But you didn't file charges. Why?

284
00:28:30,680 --> 00:28:32,960
There wasn't enough evidence
to hold Peng accountable.

285
00:28:33,040 --> 00:28:35,840
Do you remember
who was in charge of the case?

286
00:28:37,880 --> 00:28:41,040
It was a long time ago.
I don't remember clearly.

287
00:28:42,360 --> 00:28:44,720
But if you want to know,
I can look it up for you.

288
00:28:46,880 --> 00:28:48,280
- Thank you so much.
- Of course.

289
00:28:49,600 --> 00:28:50,720
I'll contact you.

290
00:28:51,320 --> 00:28:52,360
Thank you again.

291
00:28:59,040 --> 00:29:01,600
INVESTIGATING OFFICER

292
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:10,560
Still haven't given up on this case?

293
00:29:13,360 --> 00:29:14,680
I still can't let it go.

294
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:19,160
How are things on your end?

295
00:29:26,120 --> 00:29:27,360
Oab asked me to get engaged.

296
00:29:31,120 --> 00:29:33,200
I don't want things
to go any further than this.

297
00:29:35,440 --> 00:29:36,640
Does Dom know?

298
00:29:39,400 --> 00:29:40,560
I haven't told him.

299
00:29:41,760 --> 00:29:42,920
I don't dare tell him.

300
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:47,280
Things are already bad enough as they are.

301
00:29:51,120 --> 00:29:52,000
I agree.

302
00:29:52,800 --> 00:29:55,680
Don't tell him. No man could handle that.

303
00:30:00,880 --> 00:30:02,320
It'll be over soon anyway.

304
00:30:05,760 --> 00:30:06,920
I'm afraid

305
00:30:07,960 --> 00:30:10,680
Dom and I will be over
before this mission is done.

306
00:30:36,360 --> 00:30:37,800
If you're exhausted,

307
00:30:38,680 --> 00:30:40,160
take a day off, okay?

308
00:30:53,680 --> 00:30:54,720
Hey.

309
00:31:10,560 --> 00:31:11,400
What are you doing here?

310
00:31:13,480 --> 00:31:14,320
I'm meeting an investor.

311
00:31:18,560 --> 00:31:19,920
- Oh.
- Hello, Sir.

312
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:23,520
Hello. Don't be so formal.
We know each other. Sit down.

313
00:31:24,360 --> 00:31:25,440
Thank you.

314
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:29,080
- How have you been?
- I've been well, Sir.

315
00:31:29,160 --> 00:31:30,120
And who is this?

316
00:31:31,760 --> 00:31:33,720
My new subordinate. His name is Dom.

317
00:31:34,720 --> 00:31:35,800
Not replacing Pong, right?

318
00:31:36,640 --> 00:31:38,160
- No, Sir.
- Okay.

319
00:31:39,400 --> 00:31:41,840
So, what new investment
do you have for me today?

320
00:31:44,760 --> 00:31:45,840
Where are you going, Miss?

321
00:31:45,920 --> 00:31:48,280
I'm just going to the salon.
Why follow me?

322
00:31:49,000 --> 00:31:49,920
<i>You know, Miss.</i>

323
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:50,920
- My daughter.
<i>- You need us with you whenever…</i>

324
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:53,320
I spoiled her,
so she turned out like this.

325
00:31:54,640 --> 00:31:56,280
Dad, I was just going to…

326
00:32:01,520 --> 00:32:02,480
Sorry.

327
00:32:03,480 --> 00:32:05,000
I didn't know you had a guest.

328
00:32:07,160 --> 00:32:08,880
You're not having your men drive you?

329
00:32:10,240 --> 00:32:11,640
I can go later.

330
00:32:13,720 --> 00:32:15,600
I'll stay and listen
to your discussion first

331
00:32:16,760 --> 00:32:18,320
Up to you. This is Oab.

332
00:32:19,320 --> 00:32:22,040
I remember Oab.

333
00:32:23,120 --> 00:32:24,520
But I don't recognize…

334
00:32:27,280 --> 00:32:28,880
the other one.

335
00:32:30,600 --> 00:32:33,880
This is Dom. He works for me.

336
00:32:38,520 --> 00:32:40,880
Keep talking. I'll listen too.

337
00:32:40,960 --> 00:32:44,160
Yes. Well, I found

338
00:32:45,160 --> 00:32:47,480
a piece of land, Sir.
It's a great location.

339
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:49,280
But I don't have enough capital

340
00:32:49,360 --> 00:32:52,200
to invest alone,
so I wanted to ask for your advice.

341
00:32:52,280 --> 00:32:54,240
Wow.

342
00:32:55,160 --> 00:32:56,200
Where is it?

343
00:32:56,280 --> 00:32:57,480
Around Pinklao.

344
00:32:58,000 --> 00:33:00,480
The city is expanding that way,

345
00:33:00,560 --> 00:33:02,160
and a shopping mall is being built there.

346
00:33:02,240 --> 00:33:04,680
So I wanted to ask

347
00:33:04,760 --> 00:33:08,480
if you'd be interested in partnering
with me to develop a housing project.

348
00:33:08,560 --> 00:33:09,480
I'm interested.

349
00:33:12,560 --> 00:33:16,040
Building and selling houses
can be very profitable.

350
00:33:18,720 --> 00:33:20,960
Can I look over this project myself?

351
00:33:22,320 --> 00:33:23,440
You want to handle it?

352
00:33:24,840 --> 00:33:27,200
Then discuss the details with him.

353
00:33:27,800 --> 00:33:30,040
If you think it's worth investing in,
go ahead.

354
00:33:31,040 --> 00:33:33,520
I happen to have another meeting,
so I'll excuse myself.

355
00:33:33,600 --> 00:33:34,600
Yes, Sir.

356
00:33:34,680 --> 00:33:36,280
If you have any questions, talk to Plern.

357
00:33:36,360 --> 00:33:37,560
- Yes, Sir.
- Take care of it with her.

358
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:38,600
Thank you.

359
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:40,880
I'm leaving, Dear.

360
00:33:48,760 --> 00:33:49,680
Oab.

361
00:33:49,760 --> 00:33:52,560
I'll take a closer look at the details.
But in the meantime,

362
00:33:53,360 --> 00:33:55,480
can I borrow one of your men?

363
00:33:57,480 --> 00:33:58,400
One of my men?

364
00:33:58,480 --> 00:33:59,600
Yeah.

365
00:33:59,680 --> 00:34:03,240
My dad's men only listen to him.
They don't listen to me.

366
00:34:03,320 --> 00:34:06,040
I'm old enough to take care of myself,
but they still treat me like a child.

367
00:34:06,120 --> 00:34:07,200
Sure.

368
00:34:08,760 --> 00:34:10,239
But I'll need your investment.

369
00:34:11,960 --> 00:34:15,320
We'll have to see
whether I approve of your project.

370
00:34:16,600 --> 00:34:18,920
Fine. I'll arrange someone for you.

371
00:34:21,560 --> 00:34:23,080
I want this one.

372
00:34:25,800 --> 00:34:26,880
Dom is not available.

373
00:34:26,960 --> 00:34:29,480
He's a fighter I'm training.
He has to practice every day.

374
00:34:30,080 --> 00:34:32,199
Then I'm not approving your project.

375
00:34:33,440 --> 00:34:34,320
Plern.

376
00:34:34,400 --> 00:34:36,480
I don't wake up early anyway.

377
00:34:37,520 --> 00:34:38,760
He can come after training.

378
00:34:45,800 --> 00:34:47,120
Then come over after training.

379
00:34:48,719 --> 00:34:49,719
Look after Plern for me.

380
00:34:53,280 --> 00:34:54,600
When do you want to start?

381
00:34:57,080 --> 00:34:58,000
Today.

382
00:35:11,560 --> 00:35:14,440
You want me to look after that woman?
I'm not doing it.

383
00:35:16,560 --> 00:35:18,440
Dom, I don't like this either.

384
00:35:20,440 --> 00:35:21,480
But I really need the money.

385
00:35:22,360 --> 00:35:24,200
Don't you have any other investors?

386
00:35:26,560 --> 00:35:28,840
I do, but she has the most money.

387
00:35:28,920 --> 00:35:32,360
This time I really need a lot of funding.
It has to be her.

388
00:35:39,840 --> 00:35:41,720
You know how expensive it is
to run a boxing camp.

389
00:35:42,840 --> 00:35:47,600
The prize money we split with the fighters
isn't enough to keep the camp running.

390
00:35:50,320 --> 00:35:51,560
And if one day

391
00:35:52,480 --> 00:35:56,360
I let you guys run the bar and den,
but keep the boxing camp,

392
00:35:58,040 --> 00:35:59,680
I'll need money from somewhere else.

393
00:36:05,680 --> 00:36:07,520
Anyway, I'm trusting you with my future.

394
00:36:18,720 --> 00:36:20,160
You could've told me.

395
00:36:21,080 --> 00:36:22,040
Why do I have to do this?

396
00:36:22,640 --> 00:36:24,520
So your work hours depend on me.

397
00:36:26,240 --> 00:36:28,560
I'll decide when you're done for the day.

398
00:36:29,680 --> 00:36:30,680
Where are you going?

399
00:36:31,640 --> 00:36:32,560
To wash my hair.

400
00:36:33,160 --> 00:36:34,680
Can't you wash it at home?

401
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:36,920
I can.

402
00:36:39,080 --> 00:36:40,480
But I want to go to a salon.

403
00:36:49,840 --> 00:36:51,120
All done.

404
00:36:59,600 --> 00:37:02,600
Please wait a moment
and let your hair cool down.

405
00:37:02,680 --> 00:37:03,760
Okay.

406
00:37:08,560 --> 00:37:10,720
You read magazines like this?

407
00:37:17,560 --> 00:37:18,760
No answer.

408
00:37:22,280 --> 00:37:23,440
Where are you going next?

409
00:37:24,160 --> 00:37:25,360
For a walk.

410
00:37:27,040 --> 00:37:28,160
Where?

411
00:37:28,240 --> 00:37:29,360
The beach.

412
00:37:30,520 --> 00:37:31,600
The beach?

413
00:37:32,920 --> 00:37:35,400
- Today?
- Why?

414
00:37:35,920 --> 00:37:36,840
Can't we go?

415
00:37:38,400 --> 00:37:39,360
Tomorrow is my day off.

416
00:37:39,440 --> 00:37:41,000
I'm not giving you the day off.

417
00:37:43,200 --> 00:37:44,280
Hey.

418
00:37:44,360 --> 00:37:47,720
I've trained every morning for days.
Can I rest before we go to the beach?

419
00:37:47,800 --> 00:37:50,960
Besides, driving to the beach
and back in one day is exhausting.

420
00:37:51,040 --> 00:37:53,200
Who said we're going there
and back in one day?

421
00:38:01,640 --> 00:38:02,640
Then let's do this.

422
00:38:02,720 --> 00:38:05,400
I'll drive you home so you can rest.

423
00:38:06,280 --> 00:38:09,080
Then tomorrow morning, come pick me up.

424
00:38:20,040 --> 00:38:21,040
Hey.

425
00:38:23,080 --> 00:38:24,000
Where's Oab?

426
00:38:24,520 --> 00:38:26,880
He came back and went after some girl.

427
00:38:28,920 --> 00:38:30,200
And you didn't go with him?

428
00:38:30,800 --> 00:38:33,600
Maybe he didn't want me
getting in the way.

429
00:38:34,200 --> 00:38:37,400
Could be. So where's Dom?

430
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:44,080
Oab is sending him as a bodyguard
for Mr. Pinit's daughter.

431
00:38:46,480 --> 00:38:49,320
Who's Mr. Pinit?

432
00:38:49,840 --> 00:38:52,040
An investor. A businessman.

433
00:38:52,880 --> 00:38:54,320
He's a financial wizard.

434
00:38:54,400 --> 00:38:56,560
He's one of the top names
in the Thai stock market.

435
00:38:58,560 --> 00:39:00,640
- He's rich.
- But he launders money.

436
00:39:01,720 --> 00:39:03,680
He's close with all the powerful people.

437
00:39:03,760 --> 00:39:05,360
He takes that money and invests it

438
00:39:05,440 --> 00:39:07,560
until it becomes clean money.

439
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:11,200
But what surprises me is,

440
00:39:12,240 --> 00:39:14,400
he has plenty of men already.

441
00:39:14,920 --> 00:39:16,920
Why does he want Dom as a bodyguard?

442
00:39:34,440 --> 00:39:35,400
Thanks.

443
00:40:14,240 --> 00:40:15,160
Get in the car.

444
00:40:20,680 --> 00:40:21,440
Dom!

445
00:40:50,360 --> 00:40:51,680
Who do you work for?

446
00:40:54,640 --> 00:40:56,640
I asked who you work for.

447
00:40:57,560 --> 00:40:58,640
What do you want?

448
00:41:01,280 --> 00:41:03,760
Probably my father's rivals.

449
00:41:04,680 --> 00:41:05,600
They're here to get me.

450
00:41:15,560 --> 00:41:16,720
Get in the car.

451
00:41:25,680 --> 00:41:28,560
That's why Dad won't let me go out alone.
He's afraid this will happen.

452
00:41:29,080 --> 00:41:30,600
And you still snuck out.

453
00:41:35,120 --> 00:41:35,960
Does it hurt?

454
00:41:36,960 --> 00:41:37,800
Huh?

455
00:41:39,560 --> 00:41:41,280
Does the stab wound hurt?

456
00:41:46,160 --> 00:41:47,000
No.

457
00:41:48,040 --> 00:41:50,720
Stay home today and don't go out anymore.

458
00:41:53,880 --> 00:41:56,640
- Where are you going?
- To get medicine and treat your wound.

459
00:41:56,720 --> 00:41:59,800
Even if it's not serious,
it's better to clean it first.

460
00:42:11,320 --> 00:42:12,280
I'll do it myself.

461
00:42:15,600 --> 00:42:17,040
I'll do it myself.

462
00:42:36,480 --> 00:42:37,720
It really doesn't hurt?

463
00:42:42,160 --> 00:42:43,960
Don't get others hurt
because of you again.

464
00:42:53,360 --> 00:42:54,680
Stay home.

465
00:42:55,400 --> 00:42:57,320
Don't go anywhere
without someone with you.

466
00:42:58,160 --> 00:43:00,960
If you're going to be a burden,
at least be a burden who listens.

467
00:43:29,520 --> 00:43:30,360
Fon.

468
00:43:39,240 --> 00:43:40,240
Let's go home.

469
00:43:41,320 --> 00:43:42,440
Yes.

470
00:44:04,480 --> 00:44:05,680
Thank you.

471
00:44:23,960 --> 00:44:25,840
This time,
I think we can finally take Oab down.

472
00:44:25,920 --> 00:44:27,920
We've never gotten this close
to him before.

473
00:44:28,000 --> 00:44:29,960
With both Dom and Fon involved,

474
00:44:31,120 --> 00:44:33,600
and with them wanting to close this case,

475
00:44:34,800 --> 00:44:36,960
they'll probably do what we ask.

476
00:44:38,360 --> 00:44:40,360
Once we take over his territory

477
00:44:40,440 --> 00:44:41,880
and he's no longer in our way,

478
00:44:42,520 --> 00:44:45,320
our business can expand freely.

479
00:44:51,400 --> 00:44:55,000
Fon, give me a moment.
I'll make something for you to eat.

480
00:44:55,080 --> 00:44:56,560
I'm not hungry.

481
00:45:00,240 --> 00:45:01,760
I'll head upstairs.

482
00:45:02,400 --> 00:45:03,320
Okay.

483
00:45:50,280 --> 00:45:51,720
How long have you been waiting here?

484
00:45:52,720 --> 00:45:54,040
Did anyone see you?

485
00:45:56,800 --> 00:45:57,720
Dom.

486
00:45:58,680 --> 00:45:59,720
Dom!

487
00:46:03,480 --> 00:46:04,400
Why?

488
00:46:05,400 --> 00:46:06,640
Why what?

489
00:46:07,240 --> 00:46:09,320
I asked if anyone saw you.

490
00:46:11,080 --> 00:46:12,080
No one did.

491
00:46:17,400 --> 00:46:19,080
So I can't kiss you anymore?

492
00:46:21,120 --> 00:46:22,000
You can.

493
00:46:22,080 --> 00:46:24,920
But not like this. It's too risky.

494
00:46:25,000 --> 00:46:26,920
What if someone sees us?

495
00:46:27,960 --> 00:46:31,080
What if Oab finds out? You'll be dead.

496
00:46:35,120 --> 00:46:37,040
- I'm being unreasonable, aren't I?
- Yes.

497
00:46:37,760 --> 00:46:41,080
You're being very unreasonable right now.
You're not thinking ahead.

498
00:46:42,120 --> 00:46:45,200
If something happened to you,
what would I do?

499
00:46:45,800 --> 00:46:46,680
You'd be fine.

500
00:46:48,000 --> 00:46:52,200
From what I saw yesterday,
Oab seems to take good care of you too.

501
00:46:56,520 --> 00:46:57,360
Yesterday?

502
00:46:59,560 --> 00:47:01,680
Yes. Yesterday.

503
00:47:36,960 --> 00:47:37,920
Fon.

504
00:47:39,320 --> 00:47:40,680
I made you a sandwich.

505
00:47:46,800 --> 00:47:47,960
Fon.

506
00:47:54,320 --> 00:47:56,240
I'll leave it outside your door.

507
00:48:28,560 --> 00:48:30,040
Are you avoiding me?

508
00:48:34,680 --> 00:48:36,920
I never thought what I did

509
00:48:39,320 --> 00:48:41,040
would make you uncomfortable.

510
00:48:46,880 --> 00:48:48,400
I'm sorry, Fon.

511
00:48:54,960 --> 00:48:56,000
I still…

512
00:48:58,360 --> 00:48:59,800
think we're the way we used to be.

513
00:49:05,920 --> 00:49:07,160
Even if you don't feel

514
00:49:08,960 --> 00:49:11,000
the same way about me anymore,

515
00:49:16,000 --> 00:49:18,520
I still feel the same about you.

516
00:49:21,240 --> 00:49:22,720
Everything is still the same.

517
00:49:29,440 --> 00:49:30,920
I still love you, Fon.

518
00:49:37,000 --> 00:49:38,040
Can you hear me?

519
00:50:42,760 --> 00:50:44,680
Hold on a second. Dom!

520
00:50:45,440 --> 00:50:46,240
Where have you been?

521
00:50:48,120 --> 00:50:50,120
Didn't you say
you were going to spar with Haw?

522
00:50:50,720 --> 00:50:52,520
Yeah, good.

523
00:50:52,600 --> 00:50:53,760
Then warm up with Dum first.

524
00:50:53,840 --> 00:50:54,680
What the hell?

525
00:50:54,760 --> 00:50:57,320
Let me rest first. You warm up with him.

526
00:51:01,000 --> 00:51:01,840
Dom.

527
00:51:02,800 --> 00:51:04,800
Man isn't a punching bag, you know.

528
00:51:07,280 --> 00:51:08,240
I'll warm up first.

529
00:51:08,320 --> 00:51:09,400
Yeah.

530
00:51:13,520 --> 00:51:14,360
Wrap your hands.

531
00:51:21,960 --> 00:51:23,680
Since Man started boxing,

532
00:51:24,280 --> 00:51:27,680
he's never lost to anyone. Except Arm.

533
00:51:30,800 --> 00:51:36,000
<i>He's got great technique, heavy hands,</i>
<i>and most importantly, he's damn fast.</i>

534
00:51:36,800 --> 00:51:37,760
<i>If it weren't for Arm,</i>

535
00:51:38,400 --> 00:51:40,520
<i>I don't think anyone</i>
<i>could've taken Man down.</i>

536
00:51:41,040 --> 00:51:42,960
<i>Oab has studied everything about him.</i>

537
00:51:43,480 --> 00:51:45,720
<i>His footwork, his punches.</i>

538
00:51:46,680 --> 00:51:49,040
<i>I bet he's even studied</i>
<i>the way he breathes.</i>

539
00:51:53,840 --> 00:51:56,040
I'm telling you,
you might actually lose to him.

540
00:52:06,240 --> 00:52:07,440
Alright, let's go.

541
00:52:27,720 --> 00:52:29,040
Dom!

542
00:52:34,760 --> 00:52:36,040
My turn next.

543
00:52:40,320 --> 00:52:41,520
Dom.

544
00:52:41,600 --> 00:52:43,760
- Yeah?
- Don't train with me tomorrow.

545
00:52:43,840 --> 00:52:45,160
Why?

546
00:52:45,240 --> 00:52:48,160
Geez, you almost killed me.

547
00:52:48,800 --> 00:52:49,640
You're hurt?

548
00:52:49,720 --> 00:52:51,240
Look at my face!

549
00:52:51,320 --> 00:52:52,840
Shit.

550
00:52:52,920 --> 00:52:55,200
You almost busted my eyebrow open.

551
00:52:59,680 --> 00:53:03,560
Sorry. I guess I held back too little.

552
00:53:03,640 --> 00:53:06,920
Whoa, you hit me with everything you had.

553
00:53:07,000 --> 00:53:08,640
Don't say you just held back too little.

554
00:53:09,360 --> 00:53:12,720
Sorry. I'll shower,
then I'll bring the medicine kit.

555
00:53:12,800 --> 00:53:14,960
Yeah, bring it and put it on me too.

556
00:53:23,200 --> 00:53:24,120
Dom.

557
00:53:33,360 --> 00:53:34,520
Want a drink?

558
00:53:35,560 --> 00:53:36,600
No, thanks.

559
00:53:40,960 --> 00:53:42,200
What's wrong with you?

560
00:53:45,760 --> 00:53:46,720
Nothing.

561
00:53:48,760 --> 00:53:50,440
Don't lie to me.

562
00:53:51,600 --> 00:53:53,960
I've seen you
since the day you first came here.

563
00:53:57,160 --> 00:53:58,200
I understand.

564
00:53:58,280 --> 00:54:02,200
To get where you are today,
you've been through a lot.

565
00:54:04,640 --> 00:54:07,440
But I think
I've been through even more than you.

566
00:54:13,320 --> 00:54:15,040
What you're going through now,

567
00:54:15,120 --> 00:54:17,600
it's slowly changing you.

568
00:54:21,280 --> 00:54:22,440
I like you, you know.

569
00:54:23,440 --> 00:54:25,200
I noticed you from day one.

570
00:54:26,240 --> 00:54:28,440
You had drive.

571
00:54:29,880 --> 00:54:31,200
You had dreams.

572
00:54:34,920 --> 00:54:36,400
And you had something that I don't.

573
00:54:41,720 --> 00:54:43,400
What do I have that you don't?

574
00:54:46,800 --> 00:54:48,160
Freedom.

575
00:54:51,840 --> 00:54:52,840
You guys have that too.

576
00:54:56,920 --> 00:54:57,760
Us?

577
00:55:01,840 --> 00:55:04,960
We have to watch our backs
everywhere we go.

578
00:55:06,280 --> 00:55:08,040
We never know who'll come after us.

579
00:55:09,080 --> 00:55:10,560
It's like being in prison.

580
00:55:11,400 --> 00:55:13,120
We could die any minute.

581
00:55:18,480 --> 00:55:19,840
I worry, man.

582
00:55:24,200 --> 00:55:27,680
I'm afraid
you'll lose your freedom like we did.

583
00:55:31,600 --> 00:55:34,640
And I'm afraid the happiness you have now

584
00:55:35,400 --> 00:55:37,280
is slowly disappearing.

585
00:55:39,880 --> 00:55:41,960
Don't let pressure,

586
00:55:42,640 --> 00:55:43,720
power,

587
00:55:43,800 --> 00:55:46,840
or anything else
take that happiness away from you.

588
00:55:50,920 --> 00:55:52,640
You can lose anything.

589
00:55:54,560 --> 00:55:56,840
But if one day you lose your happiness,

590
00:55:57,880 --> 00:55:59,000
I suggest

591
00:56:01,200 --> 00:56:02,240
you turn around

592
00:56:03,560 --> 00:56:05,000
and walk away from here.

593
00:56:09,560 --> 00:56:11,800
Go somewhere you can be happy.

594
00:56:24,840 --> 00:56:25,720
What about you?

595
00:56:26,360 --> 00:56:27,200
Me?

596
00:56:29,360 --> 00:56:30,760
I'm happy.

597
00:56:32,640 --> 00:56:34,560
Even if I don't have freedom,

598
00:56:37,160 --> 00:56:38,680
I have friendship.

599
00:56:42,960 --> 00:56:45,120
What's wrong with you?

600
00:56:46,240 --> 00:56:48,000
You haven't seemed happy lately.

601
00:56:53,280 --> 00:56:54,600
I'm probably just stressed

602
00:56:55,600 --> 00:56:57,000
about fighting Man.

603
00:56:59,520 --> 00:57:01,240
It's not strange that you're worried.

604
00:57:07,680 --> 00:57:11,000
Man is talented, but he's lost before.

605
00:57:12,760 --> 00:57:14,160
If he loses again,

606
00:57:15,560 --> 00:57:16,440
it won't be surprising.

607
00:57:19,160 --> 00:57:21,360
Oab sees something in you.

608
00:57:24,240 --> 00:57:25,360
You need to believe in yourself.

609
00:57:36,160 --> 00:57:38,040
I got what you wanted.

610
00:57:41,120 --> 00:57:42,280
Welcome to King Boxing Camp.

611
00:57:44,680 --> 00:57:46,000
Thank you.

612
00:57:47,480 --> 00:57:50,040
You made today
not as sad as I thought it would be.

613
00:57:52,760 --> 00:57:53,720
Plern.

614
00:57:54,800 --> 00:57:56,480
Who is the woman who came with Dom?

615
00:57:56,560 --> 00:57:58,320
She's the daughter of my investor.

616
00:57:58,880 --> 00:58:01,520
But it looks like she really likes Dom.

617
00:58:02,960 --> 00:58:05,200
- Can I stop doing this?
- Stop doing what?

618
00:58:05,800 --> 00:58:07,640
Being your bodyguard. Can I quit?

619
00:58:07,720 --> 00:58:08,800
Please.

620
00:58:08,880 --> 00:58:10,600
Search until we find Dech.

621
00:58:10,680 --> 00:58:11,960
You're going to search my house?

622
00:58:16,240 --> 00:58:18,720
You came all the way here.
Aren't you afraid to die?

623
00:58:20,680 --> 00:58:22,120
Or do we make a trade?

624
00:58:22,920 --> 00:58:24,880
If I was afraid, I wouldn't be here.

625
00:58:52,880 --> 00:58:55,640
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
